A1 L2: on a quicktest map, RM_Warscar's extraGenSteps carry RM_KneelingRings live, and that genstep lays slagged/posed chassis each facing the ring centre with 0..min(hospiceIntactPerMap,3) intact (minified) chassis, every intact one holding a history and unit name present in its Scribe save XML.
A2 L2: an intact chassis the RM_HospiceHaul workgiver offers to a colonist is accepted by a cradle, then takes a component, etchant and a chassis core at their stages and passes all five stages; it wakes as a player colony mech with IsColonyMechRequiringMechanitor false, no overseer, no CompOverseerSubject, every modification hediff of its history present, named for its unit; the cradle glow is off at diagnosis and on after the lights stage.
A3 L2: a failure forced at the lights stage leaves an RM_FailedChassis whose label carries the same unit name, and the cradle empties.
A4 L2: the RM_DeserterWalksIn incident fired with forced parms spawns a walking RM_AncientServitor that, under ordinary ticks (jawa/safe_advance), reaches the cradle and kneels as an intact chassis carrying its name within 6 cells of the cradle's interaction cell.
